problems.example:
test build_phase:
  set_type_override_by_type(my_driver::get_type(),
                           err_driver::get_type());
// every my_driver created after this is really an err_driver

WRONG variant: the override call is placed in the test's run_phase, after the env was built.
This is wrong because the factory only checks overrides when a component is created. By run_phase the driver already exists as a my_driver, so the override silently does nothing and the test runs without the error injection it was supposed to test.

