sample in monitor write() -> every observed txn counts

WRONG variant: the covergroup is sampled in the driver instead of the monitor.
This is wrong because the driver only sees what the testbench drove. Any transaction the DUT produces on its own, like a status update or an interrupt driven transfer, never passes through the driver and never gets counted. The monitor sees the pins, so it sees everything.

