problems.example:
my_regs.cfg = new("cfg"); cfg.build(); map.add_reg(cfg, 'h0, "RW");
adapter: reg2bus turns a reg write into a bus txn
predictor: observed bus traffic updates mirrored values
seq: status = cfg.write(status, 'hA5);

WRONG variant: no predictor, mirror updated only by frontdoor accesses from the test.
This is wrong because DUT registers change from other sources: hardware clears a status bit, a backdoor load sets a control field, another master writes the register. Without the predictor the mirror goes stale, the next mirrored read returns a value the DUT no longer holds, and the test fails on a perfectly good DUT.

